; Copyright (C) 2026 The Tecnigrafo authors
; PT10: the DXF codec of SOLID on a handwritten file (input.dxf, R2018, no tables).
; Group order as AutoCAD writes it: AcDbTrace, 10..33, 39, 210/220/230.
; A1 four vertices, z 0.
; A2 three vertices: no 13/23/33, so the fourth is the third (rapporto.md, SOLID).
; A3 extrusion (0,0,-1), z 3 on every vertex, thickness 2. OCS vertices
;    (1,0) (4,0) (1,2) (4,2); world x -> -x (ADR 0018, point 5), order kept.
; A4 groups the model does not have: transparency 440 in AcDbEntity and XDATA.
; A5 three equal vertices and a fourth apart: not all equal, so handled.
; A6 four equal vertices, A7 three equal with 13 missing: degenerate, unhandled.
; A8 extrusion (1,0,0): unhandled (ADR 0018, point 3).
; Values by hand from the rules above; ezdxf confirms the raw vertices, but
; gives (0,0) for a missing 13, so this case is not an oracle case.
D = DXF file=input.dxf
? version D -> AC1032
? units D -> 4
; PT10 makes SOLID a handled entity: until then every SOLID is unhandled.
; cambia con #677
? count D -> SOLID 5
? unhandled D -> SOLID 3
? entity D A1 -> SOLID vertex=0,0 vertex=10,0 vertex=0,5 vertex=10,5
? entity D A2 -> SOLID vertex=0,0 vertex=6,0 vertex=3,4 vertex=3,4
? entity D A3 -> SOLID vertex=-1,0 vertex=-4,0 vertex=-1,2 vertex=-4,2 thickness=2 extrusion=0,0,-1
? entity D A4 -> SOLID vertex=10,10 vertex=14,10 vertex=10,13 vertex=14,13
? entity D A5 -> SOLID vertex=20,0 vertex=20,0 vertex=20,0 vertex=25,0
? entity D A6 -> unhandled SOLID
? entity D A7 -> unhandled SOLID
? entity D A8 -> unhandled SOLID
? bbox D:A2 -> 0,0 6,4
? bbox D:A3 -> -4,0 -1,2
? snaps D:A2 -> Endpoint 0,0; Endpoint 6,0; Endpoint 3,4
? snaps D:A5 -> Endpoint 20,0; Endpoint 25,0
; The rewritten file keeps the missing 13, the z, 39 and 210 as read, the
; extrusion back in the OCS, 440 and the XDATA (ADR 0018, points 4-6).
? roundtrip D -> identical
? roundtrip D as=cadx -> identical
